x points. With the incumbent term-limited, this is an open contest with no incumbency advantage for either side.\n\nThe evidence base is thin: no general-election polls, no expert ratings, and no fundraising or market data are available for this race. Recent coverage has highlighted Alaska's growing competitiveness, including Democratic interest in the concurrent Senate race, which supports a modest shift toward Democrats. Even so, the structural lean favors Republicans, and the wide uncertainty reflects how little hard data exists this far into the cycle.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2436, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3013, "margin": -5.5}]}